}
Cache Lifecycle Summary
Event	Cache Behavior
Query executed	Data stored in cache
Component unmounts	Cache timer starts
Component remounts (cache valid)	Returns cached data
Component remounts (cache expired)	Fetches fresh data
Mutation with invalidating tag	Cache marked stale, refetch triggered
refetch() called	Force refetch regardless of cache state
Key Takeaways
Cache is automatic - No manual cache management needed
Cache keys are unique - Based on endpoint + arguments
Tags control invalidation - Mutations invalidate queries via tags
Configurable lifetime - keepUnusedDataFor controls how long data stays
Subscribers matter - Cache is cleared only after ALL subscribers unmount + timer expires
